.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt EVP_SIGNATURE-ECDSA 7ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm EVP_SIGNATURE-ECDSA
.Nd The EVP_PKEY ECDSA signature implementation
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Support for computing ECDSA signatures.
See
.Xr EVP_PKEY-EC 7
for information related to EC keys.
.Ss Algorithm Names
In this list, names are grouped together to signify that they are the
same algorithm having multiple names.
This also includes the OID in canonical decimal form (which means that
they are possible to fetch if the caller has a mere OID which came out
in this form after a call to
.Xr OBJ_obj2txt 3 Ns ).
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It \(dqECDSA"
The base signature algorithm, supported explicitly fetched with
.Xr EVP_PKEY_sign_init_ex2 3 ,
and implicitly fetched (through
.Xr EVP_PKEY-EC 7 )
with
.Xr EVP_DigestSignInit 3
and
.Xr EVP_DigestVerifyInit 3 .
.Pp
It can't be used with
.Xr EVP_PKEY_sign_message_init 3
.It \(dqECDSA-SHA1", \(dqECDSA-SHA-1", \(dqecdsa-with-SHA1", \(dq1.2.840.10045.4.1"
.It \(dqECDSA-SHA2-224", \(dqECDSA-SHA224", \(dqecdsa-with-SHA224", \(dq1.2.840.10045.4.3.1"
.It \(dqECDSA-SHA2-256", \(dqECDSA-SHA256", \(dqecdsa-with-SHA256", \(dq1.2.840.10045.4.3.2"
.It \(dqECDSA-SHA2-384", \(dqECDSA-SHA384", \(dqecdsa-with-SHA384", \(dq1.2.840.10045.4.3.3"
.It \(dqECDSA-SHA2-512", \(dqECDSA-SHA512", \(dqecdsa-with-SHA512", \(dq1.2.840.10045.4.3.4"
.It \(dqECDSA-SHA3-224", \(dqecdsa_with_SHA3-224", \(dqid-ecdsa-with-sha3-224", \(dq2.16.840.1.101.3.4.3.9"
.It \(dqECDSA-SHA3-256", \(dqecdsa_with_SHA3-256", \(dqid-ecdsa-with-sha3-256", \(dq2.16.840.1.101.3.4.3.10"
.It \(dqECDSA-SHA3-384", \(dqecdsa_with_SHA3-384", \(dqid-ecdsa-with-sha3-384", \(dq2.16.840.1.101.3.4.3.11"
.It \(dqECDSA-SHA3-512", \(dqecdsa_with_SHA3-512", \(dqid-ecdsa-with-sha3-512", \(dq2.16.840.1.101.3.4.3.12"
ECDSA signature schemes with diverse message digest algorithms.
They are all supported explicitly fetched with
.Xr EVP_PKEY_sign_init_ex2 3
and
.Xr EVP_PKEY_sign_message_init 3 .
.El
.Ss ECDSA Signature Parameters
The following signature parameters can be set using
.Xr EVP_PKEY_CTX_set_params 3 .
This may be called after
.Xr EVP_PKEY_sign_init 3
or
.Xr EVP_PKEY_verify_init 3 ,
and before calling
.Xr EVP_PKEY_sign 3
or
.Xr EVP_PKEY_verify 3 .
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It \(dqdigest" ( Ns Sy OSSL_SIGNATURE_PARAM_DIGEST Ns ) <UTF8 string>
.It \(dqproperties" ( Ns Sy OSSL_SIGNATURE_PARAM_PROPERTIES Ns ) <UTF8 string>
These two are not supported with the ECDSA signature schemes that
already include a message digest algorithm, See
.Sx Algorithm Names
above.
.It \(dqnonce-type" ( Ns Sy OSSL_SIGNATURE_PARAM_NONCE_TYPE Ns ) <unsigned integer>
.It \(dqkey-check" ( Ns Sy OSSL_SIGNATURE_PARAM_FIPS_KEY_CHECK Ns ) <integer>
.It \(dqdigest-check" ( Ns Sy OSSL_SIGNATURE_PARAM_FIPS_DIGEST_CHECK Ns ) <integer>
These parameters are described in
.Xr provider-signature 7 .
.El
.Pp
The following signature parameters can be retrieved using
.Xr EVP_PKEY_CTX_get_params 3 .
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It \(dqalgorithm-id" ( Ns Sy OSSL_SIGNATURE_PARAM_ALGORITHM_ID Ns ) <octet string>
.It \(dqdigest" ( Ns Sy OSSL_SIGNATURE_PARAM_DIGEST Ns ) <UTF8 string>
.It \(dqnonce-type" ( Ns Sy OSSL_SIGNATURE_PARAM_NONCE_TYPE Ns ) <unsigned integer>
.It \(dqfips-indicator" ( Ns Sy OSSL_SIGNATURE_PARAM_FIPS_APPROVED_INDICATOR Ns ) <integer>
.It \(dqverify-message" ( Ns Sy OSSL_SIGNATURE_PARAM_FIPS_VERIFY_MESSAGE No <integer>
The parameters are described in
.Xr provider-signature 7 .
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr EVP_PKEY_CTX_set_params 3 ,
.Xr EVP_PKEY_sign 3 ,
.Xr EVP_PKEY_verify 3 ,
.Xr provider-signature 7 ,
